## 2026-07-30 - Deleted-document re-upload frontend investigation

Investigation only. No frontend fix was implemented.

### Findings

- `frontend/src/services/api.ts:246-277` creates a fresh idempotency key per upload
  action, submits to `/api/documents/upload`, polls the ingestion job, and converts
  a failed job into an `ApiError`.
- The fresh-key behavior is correct and prevents re-selecting a deleted file from
  replaying the old completed job.
- The queue request returns HTTP 202. The actual failure is asynchronous in the
  backend worker, so it is not available in the initial upload response.
- The backend returns only `internal_processing_error` and
  `Document processing failed.` for the confirmed SQLite failure.
- `frontend/src/components/UploadDocumentsModal.tsx:150-190` displays that safe
  generic message, marks the item failed, and offers Retry Failed.
- Retrying starts another upload action. Because the database constraint is
  deterministic and terminal, retry cannot resolve it and may add another failed
  document/version/content row and retained stored file.
- HTTP 409 is treated as skipped/duplicate, but this incident is reported as a
  polled HTTP-422-style `ApiError`, so the UI correctly labels it failed rather
  than duplicate.
- Delete calls `DELETE /documents/{id}` and refreshes the library. The recently
  deleted list exposes restore. No frontend cache or filename check blocks
  re-upload.
- Error parsing for immediate API failures expects a string `detail`; job failures
  use the separate structured job error path and are handled.

### Frontend impact of the recommended backend fix

- No API shape change is required. Upload can remain 202 plus polling.
- On successful backend correction, same-content re-upload should complete and the
  existing UI will show success.
- If a stable lifecycle conflict code is introduced, map it to an actionable,
  non-sensitive message and do not expose content hashes, deleted-document IDs,
  owner existence, SQL text, or storage keys.
- Disable or relabel automatic retry for terminal non-retryable job codes. Retry
  should remain available for explicitly transient dependency failures.
- Add an end-to-end UI test for delete, re-select the same file, polling completion,
  and library refresh.

